    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92295" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέμβ-ω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn round and round</i>, 
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέμβει: πλανᾶται</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.134
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, aor.
			inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥεμφθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέμβομαι</span></b> , <i>roam, rove,
				roll about</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				481.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				447.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.Euerg.
				3J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1581.6
			</span></i><span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				62.7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξω ῥ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Pr.</u>
				7.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ τοῦ στρατοπέδου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Fab.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Πειραιεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Dem.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰν ἁλί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.415
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμμασι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.288
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): metaph., <i>to be unsteady, act at random</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς πράγμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν εἰδώλοις καὶ σκιαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.80f
				</span></i>
			; of food eaten without an appetite, ib. <i><span class="en">
				664a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέμβεται ἡ λέξις</span>
			<i>is vague</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				2.52
			</span></i>. (Cf. Lith. <i>reñgtis</i> 'bend, curve
			(intr.)'.)</div>
